# p_6d3b — Ines at the floor, evening gathers at the coffee table

A fresh document built around two strong patterns the library has been splitting across competing hypotheses. First, Ines's laptop is on the office floor (floor_o_o1) during work, while her charger, headphones, pen, and water bottle stay on the desk beside her. The 03:00 pass caught the laptop at both floor and desk (x1 each), but the 17:00 and 18:00 passes confirm floor; the desk items (charger at 15/17/18, headphones at 15/16/17/18, water bottle at 15/17/18) are consistently at desk_o1. Second, the evening (21:00–23:00) is a gathering at the coffee table: the remote, blanket, snack bowl, and Ines's mug all converge there, while the speaker sits on the couch. This is distinct from p_f7b3 (which puts snacks at the kitchen table) and from p_a3f7 (which puts everything on the couch or TV stand).

What sets this apart: the coffee_table is the evening hub (not the couch, not the kitchen table). The remote leaves the TV stand at 21:00, not 20:00. Ines's mug is at the coffee table at 22:00 (sighting confirms). The yoga mat is at bed_b1 in the early morning (the "worst objects" list shows bed_b1 twice where the library predicted coffee_table).

